# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What does not belong in the repo.
#
# The rule of thumb: anything that is downloaded, built, generated by a run, or
# specific to one machine stays out. What is left is the source, the docs and
# the recipes needed to reproduce the rest.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Model weights. 100+ GB, fetched on first start from the repo named in .env.
models/

# The Python environment start.bat builds, and anything compiled into it.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Locally built wheels (the README explains how to make them again).
wheels/*
!wheels/README.md

# Vendored third-party applications - a 300 MB portable .exe is not source.
apps/

# Runtime state: logs, marker files, the packaged output of build.ps1.
logs/
.simplex/
dist/
build/
*.spec

# Machine-specific configuration and credentials. .env.example is the template
# that IS tracked; .env itself holds this box's paths, ports and GPU sizes, and
# providers.json holds API keys for any remote endpoint that has been added.
.env
providers.json
tools/providers.json

# Conversations, the agent's scratch folder, and staging for deletion. These
# are personal working state, not part of the project.
sessions/
workspace/
_to_delete/
Claude outputs/

# Results produced by a run. Reproduce them with bench.bat / test_kv.bat rather
# than committing one machine's numbers.
bench_vram.json
bench_vram.md
bench_vram.dryrun.json
bench_vram.dryrun.md
kv_cache_tests.json

# OS and editor droppings.
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
